{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015LtC6A4cKYDc71zzF3E3uD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** GNU coreutils lack formal specifications accessible to implementers. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (one package per utility), `pkg/testutils` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format` (output formatting), `pkg/hashutil`, `pkg/sizeparse`, `pkg/encutil`, `magefiles/` (build automation).\n\n**Current state:** All 114 SRDs are spec-complete. All requirement states show \"ready\" — no code has been generated yet in this run (run 44). Package contracts exist for testutils, sys, format, hashutil, sizeparse, and encutil. Releases 00.0 through 15.0 are all spec-complete with code status \"not started.\"\n\n**Current release focus:** Release 00.0 (foundational infrastructure) is the earliest incomplete release. Use cases: magefiles (implemented), format (not started), sys (implemented), testutils (not started), hashutil (implemented), sizeparse (implemented), encutil (implemented). So the remaining work is `pkg/format` and `pkg/testutils`.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 00.0 has two use cases with code status \"not started\":\n- `rel00.0-uc002-format` → `pkg/format/` (srd003-format)\n- `rel00.0-uc004-testutils` → `pkg/testutils/` (srd001-testutils)\n\n`pkg/testutils` has no dependencies on other pkg/ packages per its import constraints. `pkg/format` depends on `pkg/sys` (which is implemented). Both are independent of each other. Since testutils is consumed by every cmd/ test, it should come first.\n\nI need to check the SRD requirements and weights for srd001-testutils and srd003-format before proposing tasks. Let me look at what's available from the requirement_states — but I notice srd001-testutils and srd003-format are not listed in requirement_states. The requirement_states only show srd004+ onwards. This means I need to read the SRD files to understand the requirements and weights.\n\nLet me read the SRD files to get the requirement details and weights."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60381,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":60381},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c01ef8fc-8a66-448d-af06-27f5898a2cc4","uuid":"4870ce3a-19ac-4b05-918b-143d88895d79"}
